  <body>
    <main>
      <span class="wip">work in progress</span>
      <h1>mlx-beam</h1>
      <p class="lead">B.E.A.M. — Batched Engine for Apple Metal. An MLX inference engine for hybrid-attention and mixture-of-experts models on Apple silicon.</p>

      <h2>Install</h2>
      <pre><code>uv tool install "mlx-beam @ git+https://github.com/p4ik/mlx-beam"
beam doctor</code></pre>

      <h2>What it is built for</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A prefix cache with recurrent-state checkpoints — long conversations resume from disk instead of re-prefilling.</li>
        <li>Multi-token prediction inside continuous batching.</li>
        <li>Expert streaming from SSD with a resident pool, for models larger than RAM.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Today</h2>
      <p>The skeleton: packaging, CI on Apple silicon, <code>beam doctor</code>. Nothing serves a model yet. Measured numbers will appear here when there are some.</p>

      <footer>
        <a href="https://github.com/p4ik/mlx-beam">GitHub</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/p4ik/mlx-beam/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">Changelog</a> ·
        Apache-2.0
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
